    "ExplanationCorrect": "Under marginal cost of capital analysis, projects are accepted as long as the project's IRR exceeds the marginal cost of the capital required to fund it. The optimal capital budget is determined by the intersection of the investment opportunity schedule (IOS — projects ranked by descending IRR) and the marginal cost of capital (MCC) schedule. Alpha: $8M, IRR 15.5% > 10.00% → accept. Cost: 10.00% on first $8M. Beta: $12M, IRR 13.0%. First $7M of Beta (bringing cumulative to $15M) costs 10.00%. Remaining $5M of Beta costs 12.00%. Since Beta's IRR (13.0%) > 12.00% → accept. Gamma: $6M, IRR 11.5%. Cumulative capital raises to $26M — within the 12.00% tier ($15M–$27M). IRR 11.5% < 12.00% → reject. Delta: IRR 9.0% < 10.00% (lowest tier) → reject. Optimal budget: $20M (Alpha + Beta). The MCC schedule steps up as the firm exhausts lower-cost capital sources — retained earnings at lower cost give way to new equity issuance at higher cost due to flotation costs and information asymmetry.",
