    "ExplanationWrongC": "DFL is not Total Assets / EBIT ($80M / $16M = 5.0). This ratio approximates the asset turnover, which measures operating efficiency, not financial leverage sensitivity. The correct formula involves the relationship between EBIT and earnings available to common shareholders, as captured by the interest expense. DFL = EBIT / (EBIT − Interest) focuses on the amplification from fixed financing costs, not from asset scale.",
