    "ExplanationWrongC": "The Gordon Growth Model values the entire infinite stream of future dividends from t = 1 onward, not just dividends from year 5. Computing D₅ / (r − g) would value dividends from year 6 onward (D₆, D₇, ...), which must then be discounted back 5 years to present value. Using D₅ in the numerator without discounting is incorrect. The standard formula P₀ = D₁ / (r − g) already captures all future dividends, including the terminal value of the perpetuity, in a single step.",
