    "ExplanationWrongC": "Doubling the discount rate is arbitrary and lacks theoretical foundation. A country risk premium should be estimated based on observable data — sovereign bond yield spreads, country credit ratings, or the volatility of the country's equity market relative to global markets. Doubling WACC from 9% to 18% would disproportionately penalize the project's long-term cash flows (an additional 9% annual erosion may be far more than the actual risk warrants). The correct approach estimates the premium from market data rather than applying an ad hoc multiplier.",
