    "ExplanationWrongD": "Portfolio beta does NOT require correlation data — it is a value-weighted average of individual betas. Correlation between securities affects portfolio variance (total risk) and the benefits of diversification, but beta itself is additive when value-weighted. The CAPM defines beta as the measure of systematic risk, and portfolio beta is the weighted sum of component betas.",
