    "ExplanationCorrect": "DIO = Average Inventory / (COGS/365) = $3.5M / ($25.55M/365) = $3.5M / $70,000 = 50.0 days. DSO = Average AR / (Revenue/365) = $3.8M / ($36.5M/365) = $3.8M / $100,000 = 38.0 days. DPO = Average AP / (COGS/365) = $3.08M / $70,000 = 44.0 days. CCC = DIO + DSO − DPO = 50 + 38 − 44 = 44 days. This means Avalon takes 44 days on average from paying suppliers for inventory to collecting cash from customers — the period during which the firm must finance its operations. A shorter CCC reduces the need for external financing and improves liquidity. The three levers to reduce CCC: reduce DIO (faster inventory turnover), reduce DSO (faster collection), or increase DPO (slower payment to suppliers). Each has trade-offs: aggressive DPO extension may damage supplier relationships or forfeit early payment discounts.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "DPO of 31 days results from using revenue instead of COGS: $3.08M/($36.5M/365) = $3.08M/$100,000 = 30.8 ≈ 31 days. But payables arise from inventory purchases, which are measured at cost (COGS), not at selling price (revenue). The correct denominator is daily COGS ($25.55M/365 = $70,000), yielding DPO = $3.08M/$70,000 = 44 days. Using revenue understates DPO and overstates CCC, making the firm's cash cycle appear worse than it is.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "DIO of 35 days results from using revenue instead of COGS: $3.5M/($36.5M/365) = $3.5M/$100,000 = 35 days. Inventory is carried at cost on the balance sheet and flows through COGS on the income statement — the matching principle requires using COGS, not revenue, to compute inventory turnover. The correct DIO is 50 days, and the correct CCC is 44 days.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "CCC of 132 days results from adding all three components (50+38+44=132) instead of subtracting DPO (50+38−44=44). The formula is DIO + DSO − DPO because DPO represents financing provided by suppliers that REDUCES the cash conversion cycle. Adding DPO treats supplier credit as if it consumes cash rather than providing it.",
    "FormulaReference": "CCC = DIO + DSO − DPO; DIO=Avg Inv/(COGS/365); DSO=Avg AR/(Rev/365); DPO=Avg AP/(COGS/365)",
