    "Stem": "Lakeside Precision, a fabricated metals producer, is tightening working capital under a new treasury mandate. Controller Ananya Patel reports days inventory outstanding of 52 days, days sales outstanding of 41 days, and days payable outstanding of 36 days for the trailing quarter. The CFO has set a target cash conversion cycle below 55 days to free $8 million in operating cash. Ms. Patel must compute the current cash conversion cycle and assess whether the target is met. What is the correct cash conversion cycle?",
