    "UniqueConceptKey": "B-270-short-term-financing-compensating-balance-effective-cost-selection",
    "Stem": "Horizon Metals needs $900,000 for a seasonal inventory build. Treasurer Luis Alvarez has two committed options for 90 days. Option X is a bank line at 7.20% nominal with a 15% compensating balance required on the loan amount, held in a non-interest-bearing account. Option Y is commercial paper at 6.50% nominal with $4,500 in dealer fees. The CFO prioritizes minimizing the effective borrowing cost and wants to avoid understating the cost of idle balances. Which financing assessment correctly ranks the options?",
