    "ExplanationWrongB": "",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "Dealer and placement fees are a component of the cost of funds and must be amortized over the financing period. On $900,000 for 90 days, $4,500 is 50 basis points for the quarter, or about 202 basis points annualized (360-day basis). Excluding fees understates commercial paper cost by over 2 percentage points and would make Option Y appear cheaper than it is, potentially causing Horizon to choose the more expensive source.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Stated rates do not converge automatically when structural features differ. A 7.20% bank line with a 15% idle requirement and a 6.50% commercial paper instrument with upfront fees have different cash-flow patterns and therefore different effective annual rates. Market competition compresses spreads but does not erase the cost of compensating balances or transaction fees, which are contractual, not arbitrageable risk premia.",
