    "UniqueConceptKey": "B-271-long-term-financing-eps-indifference-debt-equity-analysis",
    "Stem": "Verdant Industries needs $12 million for a plant automation project. CFO Elena Ruiz is comparing two financing plans. Plan A issues 1,200,000 new common shares with no new debt. Plan B issues 800,000 shares plus $4,000,000 of 7.00% debt (annual interest $280,000). The corporate tax rate is 25% and current outstanding shares are 2,000,000, but the indifference analysis is performed on the new financing only. The board asks at what EBIT level the EPS from both plans is identical. What is the correct EBIT indifference point?",
