    "ExplanationWrongB": "Dividing interest by the debt weight (33% of $12M financing) confuses WACC weight logic with EPS indifference. Indifference depends on share counts and interest, not on the proportion of debt in total capital. The arithmetic 280k/0.50 = 560k has no derivation from the EPS equality and would mislead the board about the leverage crossover point by $280k.",
