    "Stem": "HarborView Distribution sells $36 million annually on credit with a current DSO of 48 days. Credit Manager Carla Jensen proposes tightening terms from net 45 to net 30, forecasting DSO will fall to 32 days but annual credit sales will decline by $900,000 at a 32% contribution margin, and bad-debt losses will fall by $140,000. The firm's after-tax cost of capital is 10% and the 16-day DSO improvement frees receivables investment for the full year. Ms. Jensen must recommend whether the policy change increases firm value. Which evaluation correctly weighs the trade-off?",
