    "Stem": "Brookfield Supply carries $4.20 million in receivables with terms net 60 and DSO of 52 days. The firm can factor receivables at a 1.80% discount for immediate cash, or draw on a revolving line at 7.00% per annum. Controller Maya Owens calculates the annualized cost of forgoing the factor's cash (or equivalently, the effective cost of not factoring) to compare it to the bank rate. The sales team warns that factoring may signal financial weakness to customers. Which working capital assessment correctly compares the options?",
