    "Stem": "Cascade Global operates a wholly owned subsidiary in a country where the government has recently imposed capital controls, tightened profit repatriation limits, and discussed potential expropriation of foreign-owned distribution assets. Treasury VP Nina Patel is evaluating mitigation strategies including purchasing political risk insurance, restructuring as a joint venture with a reputable local partner, and natural hedging by matching local-currency revenues with local-currency debt. The board seeks a sustainable approach that addresses both transfer risk and expropriation exposure without creating new financial risk or violating local regulations. Which international finance assessment correctly evaluates the options?",
