    "LOSTag": "B.3",
    "ItemStyle": "single-select",
    "CalculationItem": true,
    "UniqueConceptKey": "trade_credit_cost_forgo_discount",
    "Authorities": [
      "Managerial economics"
    ],
    "FormulaReference": "CB-10: Cash Conversion Cycle (CCC)",
    "CommonTrapReference": "Using 2/100 instead of 2/98 as the cost basis",
    "DecisionTreeReference": "Step 1 — discount 2%, discount period 10, net period 30. Step 2 — cost = (2/98) × (360/(30−10)). Step 3 — annualize.",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "When a firm forgoes a 2/10 net 30 discount, it effectively borrows the discounted amount (98 cents per $1 of invoice) for the extra 20 days (30 − 10). Effective annual cost = (discount % / (100 − discount %)) × (360 / (net days − discount days)) = (2/98) × (360/20) = 0.020408 × 18 = 0.36735 ≈ 36.73%. Recomputed independently: 2/98 = 0.020408; 360/20 = 18; 0.020408 × 18 = 36.73%. Forgoing the discount costs Flash Industrial roughly 37% annually — far above any reasonable bank borrowing rate — so the firm should take the discount and borrow elsewhere if it needs the extra 20 days of financing.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "Using 30 days in the denominator (360/30 = 12) gives (2/98) × 12 = 24.49%, close to the listed 24.33%. The extra credit days are the difference between the net period and the discount period: 30 − 10 = 20 days, not the full 30-day net term. Using the full net period understates the annualized cost.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "Using 2/100 instead of 2/98 as the cost basis gives (2/100) × (360/20) = 36.00%, slightly low. The cost is measured on the funds retained after the discount is forgone — the 98% of the invoice — so the periodic rate is 2/98 = 2.0408%, not 2.0000%.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Compounding the periodic rate over the year gives (1 + 2/98)^(360/20) − 1 = (1.020408)^18 − 1 ≈ 43.8%, not 44.59%. The standard exam formula uses simple annualization (periodic rate × number of periods); the compounding variant is not the convention tested here, and the listed value does not match either computation exactly.",
