    "Stem": "Crestview Manufacturing operates from a central treasury that disburses cash in uniform amounts throughout the year. The firm's annual cash requirement is $2.8 million, each cash conversion transaction costs $35, and Crestview's opportunity cost on short-term marketable securities is 5%. What is the optimal cash conversion amount under the Baumol model?",
