    "ExplanationCorrect": "The Baumol model calculates optimal cash conversion as the square root of (2 times T times F divided by O), where T is the annual cash requirement ($2,800,000), F is the fixed transaction cost ($35), and O is the opportunity cost (0.05). Calculation: the square root of (2 x 2,800,000 x 35 / 0.05) equals the square root of 3,920,000,000, which is approximately $6,261.",
