    "ExplanationCorrect": "The Hamada equation adjusts beta for leverage: βL = βU × (1 + (1 − t) × D/E). First, unlever Crockett's beta: βU = 1.26 / (1 + (1 − 0.30) × 0.50) = 1.26 / 1.35 = 0.933. Then relever for Meridian's target D/E of 60/40 = 1.50: βL = 0.933 × (1 + (1 − 0.30) × 1.50) = 0.933 × 2.05 = 1.913. Cost of equity = 3.5% + 1.913 × 6.0% = 14.98%. WACC = 0.60 × 7.5% × (1 − 0.30) + 0.40 × 14.98% = 3.15% + 5.99% = 9.14%.",
